# XML formatting arrived in CSharpier 1.0 and is not what this repository adopted it for.
# Project files are reviewed as build configuration, not as prose, and reformatting them
# buries a one-line pin change in a whole-file diff.
*.csproj
*.props
*.targets
*.config
*.slnx

# dotnet new template sources. These carry <!--#if (unionMode) --> conditionals and
# placeholder identifiers, so three of them do not parse as C# at all, and re-indenting
# the conditional comments changes what the template engine emits. Formatting them needs
# its own pass, verified with build/verify-templates.sh.
src/Templates/Hardened.Templates/templates/

# CSharpier 1.3.0 ships a Roslyn that does not parse the C# union keyword, so this file
# reports CS1001 and is left unformatted. Excluding it keeps `csharpier check` usable as a
# gate. Revisit when CSharpier picks up a Roslyn that knows the syntax.
src/IntegrationTests/Union/Hardened.IntegrationTests.Union.SUT/TodoController.cs

# Recorded generator output, compared byte for byte by the golden tests. These files are a
# record of what the generators emit, not code this repository writes, so formatting them
# fails RouteTable_OutputIsByteIdentical and SpecRouteTable_OutputIsByteIdentical. Rewrite
# them with HARDENED_RECORD_FIXTURES=1, never with a formatter.
src/SourceGenerators/Hardened.OpenApi.SourceGenerator.Tests/Fixtures/
src/SourceGenerators/Hardened.SourceGenerator.Tests/Web/Fixtures/
src/SourceGenerators/Hardened.Smithy.BuildTask.Tests/Fixtures/
